{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 495 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "c674de72212adc20ba0a4913af8e8010e27887ab77ad8cebc1e78c5978160f4f" :edb/db-before-t 494 :edb/db-after-t 495 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533807 50 #inst "2026-10-05T02:06:25.215Z" 13194139533807 true] [17592186096703 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252645 13194139533807 true] [17592186096703 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252652 13194139533807 true] [17592186096703 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252666 13194139533807 true] [17592186096703 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252673 13194139533807 true] [17592186096703 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252687 13194139533807 true] [17592186096704 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252659 13194139533807 true] [17592186096704 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252680 13194139533807 true] [17592186096704 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252694 13194139533807 true] [17592186096704 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252701 13194139533807 true] [17592186096704 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252708 13194139533807 true] [17592186252645 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252646 13194139533807 true] [17592186252645 1089 "q-112561" 13194139533807 true] [17592186252645 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533807 true] [17592186252645 1100 "Let $(x,y)$ be the solution of the following system. What is the value of $x+y?$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=7 \\\\ 0.5x+0.4y=0.2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533807 true] [17592186252645 1113 #uuid "57dc1d54-5a8e-5211-85bd-cc10abc48676" 13194139533807 true] [17592186252645 1145 "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply the second equation by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=7 &  \\\\ 0.5x+0.4y=0.2 & |\\,\\times 10\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=7 \\\\ 5x+4y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we multiply the  first equation by $-5,$ then we will get a $-5x$ term that can cancel with the $5x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=7 & |\\,\\times (-5) \\\\ 5x+4y=2\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}-5x-15y=-35 \\\\ 5x+4y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $x$-variable and allows us to solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}-\\cancel{5x}-15y & =-35 \\\\ \\cancel{5x}+4y & =2 \\\\ (-15y+4y) & =(-33) \\\\ -11y & =-33 \\\\ y & =3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $y=3$ into the equation $x+3y=7$ to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}x+3y & =7 \\\\ x+3(3) & =7 \\\\ x+9 & =7 \\\\ x & =-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-2,\\,y=3.$ So,\n\n$$\nx+y=(-2)+(3)=1.\n$$" 13194139533807 true] [17592186252646 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252647 13194139533807 true] [17592186252646 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252648 13194139533807 true] [17592186252646 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252649 13194139533807 true] [17592186252646 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252650 13194139533807 true] [17592186252646 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252651 13194139533807 true] [17592186252646 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533807 true] [17592186252646 1041 "selection" 13194139533807 true] [17592186252646 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252648 13194139533807 true] [17592186252646 1110 #uuid "feb69340-ddff-558d-8d5a-1d96eaac1c2d" 13194139533807 true] [17592186252647 1034 "-5" 13194139533807 true] [17592186252647 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533807 true] [17592186252647 1111 #uuid "50fba200-cc50-59ff-8e9d-08ef5d1a4c5c" 13194139533807 true] [17592186252648 1034 "1" 13194139533807 true] [17592186252648 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533807 true] [17592186252648 1111 #uuid "9bd2c871-f376-54ed-a302-50068a27509b" 13194139533807 true] [17592186252649 1034 "0" 13194139533807 true] [17592186252649 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533807 true] [17592186252649 1111 #uuid "2bb080ff-07ac-5d16-acdd-b55afe508236" 13194139533807 true] [17592186252650 1034 "-1" 13194139533807 true] [17592186252650 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533807 true] [17592186252650 1111 #uuid "cc2d7656-46cf-54bb-95e6-7bb2fa44ef8f" 13194139533807 true] [17592186252651 1034 "5" 13194139533807 true] [17592186252651 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533807 true] [17592186252651 1111 #uuid "cf3d11c1-9f99-5daf-8b7c-e595c728786f" 13194139533807 true] [17592186252652 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252653 13194139533807 true] [17592186252652 1089 "q-112562" 13194139533807 true] [17592186252652 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533807 true] [17592186252652 1100 "Let $(x,y)$ be the solution of the following system. What is the value of $x+y?$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+3y=15 \\\\ 0.6x-0.8y=1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533807 true] [17592186252652 1113 #uuid "98c374fa-24fb-51fc-a983-bcd8e729a379" 13194139533807 true] [17592186252652 1145 "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply the second equation by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+3y=15 &  \\\\ 0.6x-0.8y=1 & |\\,\\times 10\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}4x+3y=15 \\\\ 6x-8y=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we multiply the first equation by $3$ and the second equation by $-2,$ we will get a $12x$ term in the first equation that can cancel with the $-12x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+3y=15 & |\\,\\times 3 \\\\ 6x-8y=10 & |\\,\\times -2\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}12x+9y=45 \\\\ -12x+16y=-20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $x$-variable and allows us to solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{12x}+9y & =45 \\\\ -\\cancel{12x}+16y & =-20 \\\\ (9y+16y) & =(45-20) \\\\ 25y & =25 \\\\ y & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $y=1$ into the equation $4x+3y=15$ to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+3y & =15 \\\\ 4x+3 & =15 \\\\ 4x & =15-3 \\\\ 4x & =12 \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $x=3$ and $y=1.$ So, \n\n$$\nx+y=3+1=4.\n$$" 13194139533807 true] [17592186252653 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252654 13194139533807 true] [17592186252653 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252655 13194139533807 true] [17592186252653 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252656 13194139533807 true] [17592186252653 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252657 1319413953