0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}10a+15b-60=0 \\\\ 6a-4b-10=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we  multiply the first equation by $\\frac{2}{5}$ and the second equation by $\\frac{3}{2},$ we will get a $6b$ term in the first equation that can cancel with the $-6b$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}10a+15b-60=0 & |\\,\\times \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ 6a-4b-10=0 & |\\,\\times \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}4a+6b-24=0 \\\\ 9a-6b-15=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $b$-variable and allows us to solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4a+\\cancel{6b}-24 & =0 \\\\ 9a-\\cancel{6b}-15 & =0 \\\\ (4a+9a)+(-24-15) & =0 \\\\ 13a-39 & =0 \\\\ a & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $a=3$ into the equation $6a-4b-10=0$ to solve for $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6a-4b-10 & =0 \\\\ 6(3)-4b-10 & =0 \\\\ 18-4b-10 & =0 \\\\ 8-4b & =0 \\\\ b & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $a=3$ and $b=2.$ So, \n\n$$\na+b=3+2=5.\n$$" 13194139533807 true] [17592186252660 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252661 13194139533807 true] [17592186252660 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252662 13194139533807 true] [17592186252660 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252663 13194139533807 true] [17592186252660 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252664 13194139533807 true] [17592186252660 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252665 13194139533807 true] [17592186252660 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533807 true] [17592186252660 1041 "selection" 13194139533807 true] [17592186252660 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252665 13194139533807 true] [17592186252660 1110 #uuid "b1b8d38f-f17e-5b5e-9bbc-04881cbd3213" 13194139533807 true] [17592186252661 1034 "2" 13194139533807 true] [17592186252661 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533807 true] [17592186252661 1111 #uuid "0dce6ddb-77c5-5ad1-924a-02940711203d" 13194139533807 true] [17592186252662 1034 "1" 13194139533807 true] [17592186252662 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533807 true] [17592186252662 1111 #uuid "b33